# =============================================================================
# .gitignore
# =============================================================================
# PURPOSE: Tells Git which files must NEVER be committed to the repository.
#
# WHAT TO BUILD: Under the TODOs below, add one pattern per line, with no "#".
# Lines that start with "#" are comments, and Git ignores them.
#
# TALKS TO: Git only. It doesn't affect how the app runs.
#
# STEPS:
#   1. Ignore installed packages:   node_modules/
#      (anyone can recreate them with `npm install`)
#   2. Ignore secrets:              .env
#      (server/.env holds the Gemini API key and the MongoDB password.
#       DO commit server/.env.example, which has blank values.)
#   3. Ignore user uploads:         server/uploads/*
#      then keep the empty folder:  !server/uploads/.gitkeep
#      (voice notes and screenshots are private data)
#   4. Ignore the Vite build output: client/dist/
#   5. Optional extras: *.log, .DS_Store, Thumbs.db, .vscode/
#
# CONCEPTS TO LEARN:
#   - .gitignore pattern syntax (folder/, *.ext, !exception)
#   - Why secrets must never be pushed to GitHub
#   - `git status`, to check that a file really is ignored
# =============================================================================
